(3245033, 450965, 51538, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, and the end result looks good.  I especially like the colours.  The concept, in my opinion, of motion panning is that the camera is on a fixed location (such as in the hands or on a tripod) and can be rotated to follow a moving object.  In this case, it looks like the camera was mounted on the moving object and, therefore, not panned.  The overall effect is similar and your result is perhaps more striking.</td>', 'Nice idea, and the end result looks good.  I especially like the colours.  The concept, in my opinion, of motion panning is that the camera is on a fixed location (such as in the hands or on a tripod) and can be rotated to follow a moving object.  In this case, it looks like the camera was mounted on the moving object and, therefore, not panned.  The overall effect is similar and your result is perhaps more striking.', '2007-01-17 06:45:18.000000', NULL, 1),
