(3273662, 454082, 61930, '<td valign="top">I looked at this shot the longest I think, I was intrigued by it - wanting to know what you meant by the title and who this man was.  Interesting and thought-provoking :)</td>', 'I looked at this shot the longest I think, I was intrigued by it - wanting to know what you meant by the title and who this man was.  Interesting and thought-provoking :)', '2007-01-24 01:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3273700, 453489, 67671, '<td valign="top">I would like to thank everyone for there comments, I personally liked the tight crop, but agree the norm is to have a looking space, I feel honored to be voted 4th place, and thank you all for the time spent voting, and commenting, about the shot, this was a hand held shot, with the lens at about 150ml, about 50yds from the road, I was hoping to get some motorcycles going by, and was just taking every thing from trucks, to people walking and jogging, just practicing, when I saw this car, I think its a Shelby Cobra, not sure though as these kit cars all tend to be slightly different, just so lucky at how well it came out, this is really the first time I ever tried to get a motion pan, shots like this I always used a high shutter speed to keep the subject sharp, thanks again. Ken</td>', 'I would like to thank everyone for there comments, I personally liked the tight crop, but agree the norm is to have a looking space, I feel honored to be voted 4th place, and thank you all for the time spent voting, and commenting, about the shot, this was a hand held shot, with the lens at about 150ml, about 50yds from the road, I was hoping to get some motorcycles going by, and was just taking every thing from trucks, to people walking and jogging, just practicing, when I saw this car, I think its a Shelby Cobra, not sure though as these kit cars all tend to be slightly different, just so lucky at how well it came out, this is really the first time I ever tried to get a motion pan, shots like this I always used a high shutter speed to keep the subject sharp, thanks again. Ken', '2007-01-24 01:44:07.000000', NULL, 0),
