(3286384, 453991, 29156, '<td valign="top">you are our horse photographer, Gurry, good one</td>', 'you are our horse photographer, Gurry, good one', '2007-01-26 11:07:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3286625, 453743, 55838, '<td valign="top">I might just be inexperienced, I haven''t been at this photgraphy thing very long, but IMO this shot meets the challenge beautifully.  The foreground is certainly separate from the background.  I have not read that the foreground must be in crisp focus for an image to truly be motion panning but judging by the scores in this challenge that is the very narrow perpective held by the majority of voters.  Maybe they are technically right - who knows - who cares.  I love the artistry of this image and think it rocks &amp; is under rated.  Keep up the good work!</td>', 'I might just be inexperienced, I haven''t been at this photgraphy thing very long, but IMO this shot meets the challenge beautifully.  The foreground is certainly separate from the background.  I have not read that the foreground must be in crisp focus for an image to truly be motion panning but judging by the scores in this challenge that is the very narrow perpective held by the majority of voters.  Maybe they are technically right - who knows - who cares.  I love the artistry of this image and think it rocks & is under rated.  Keep up the good work!', '2007-01-26 11:43:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3287083, 453743, 49969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aimeethetoo:</b></div><hr/><i> The foreground is certainly separate from the background.  I have not read that the foreground must be in crisp focus for an image to truly be motion panning but judging by the scores in this challenge that is the very narrow perpective held by the majority of voters.  Maybe they are technically right - who knows - who cares.  I love the artistry of this image and think it rocks &amp; is under rated.  Keep up the good work! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i totally agree! Jeileen, there''s definitely motion panning here, otherwise the degrees of blurness wouldn''t be different between the foreground and the background. Although the perception of beauty is a very individual thing, holding fast to hard rules is not what makes photography exciting.</td>', 'Originally posted by aimeethetoo: The foreground is certainly separate from the background.  I have not read that the foreground must be in crisp focus for an image to truly be motion panning but judging by the scores in this challenge that is the very narrow perpective held by the majority of voters.  Maybe they are technically right - who knows - who cares.  I love the artistry of this image and think it rocks & is under rated.  Keep up the good work!   i totally agree! Jeileen, there''s definitely motion panning here, otherwise the degrees of blurness wouldn''t be different between the foreground and the background. Although the perception of beauty is a very individual thing, holding fast to hard rules is not what makes photography exciting.', '2007-01-26 13:33:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3287350, 453560, 32754, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, great feeling of motion and very nice composition.</td>', 'Congratulations, great feeling of motion and very nice composition.', '2007-01-26 14:39:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3287529, 452479, 18339, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the Red :)</td>', 'Congratulations on the Red :)', '2007-01-26 15:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3288147, 454141, 55838, '<td valign="top">Robbed I tell you - you was robbed!  Outstanding image.  Very artistic.  I think your commenters were much wiser than the voters at large!  Rock on!</td>', 'Robbed I tell you - you was robbed!  Outstanding image.  Very artistic.  I think your commenters were much wiser than the voters at large!  Rock on!', '2007-01-26 17:28:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3288160, 453439, 55838, '<td valign="top">WHAT??  5.08??!  I loved this shot - one of my top picks!  What were the voters thinkin''!?</td>', 'WHAT??  5.08??!  I loved this shot - one of my top picks!  What were the voters thinkin''!?', '2007-01-26 17:31:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3288629, 453743, 31341, '<td valign="top">Note:  I want to thank you all for the comments.  I would like to point out that I assure you this was panned.  It was a tele lens at 1/4 second.  If you look carefully just above the girl''s head, I cropped off a distracting light that was stretched across a large part of the picture giving you an idea of how much this was panned.  I left a little of it just so I didn''t have to crop her head too much.  I really enjoy these kind of shots.</td>', 'Note:  I want to thank you all for the comments.  I would like to point out that I assure you this was panned.  It was a tele lens at 1/4 second.  If you look carefully just above the girl''s head, I cropped off a distracting light that was stretched across a large part of the picture giving you an idea of how much this was panned.  I left a little of it just so I didn''t have to crop her head too much.  I really enjoy these kind of shots.', '2007-01-26 20:03:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3288864, 454141, 35545, '<td valign="top">This seems to be one of those love it or hate it shots.  I''m firmly in the "love it" camp.  To me, it''s the perfect combination of art and the absurd.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'This seems to be one of those love it or hate it shots.  I''m firmly in the "love it" camp.  To me, it''s the perfect combination of art and the absurd.  Keep up the good work.', '2007-01-26 21:16:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3290338, 453807, 47274, '<td valign="top">GREAT TIMING.<br/>i love the expression.<br/>p.s. real guys wear tight jeans!</td>', 'GREAT TIMING.i love the expression.p.s. real guys wear tight jeans!', '2007-01-27 08:49:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3290373, 453743, 34192, '<td valign="top">I love this image.  Many people have a particular mind-set when approaching a challenge subject.  I think this fit outside their mind set.  Their bad, not yours.  The composition, the colors, the motion, all set this image apart from most others.  You did a great job.  BTW - next time you''re in DC, drop me a line we can go out shooting...</td>', 'I love this image.  Many people have a particular mind-set when approaching a challenge subject.  I think this fit outside their mind set.  Their bad, not yours.  The composition, the colors, the motion, all set this image apart from most others.  You did a great job.  BTW - next time you''re in DC, drop me a line we can go out shooting...', '2007-01-27 09:21:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3290840, 453807, 51001, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Citadel:</b></div><hr/><i> Not really getting a feeling of panning in this shot. The guy in the background is also distracting. In fact he is the only evidence of motion in this shot (aside from the fact that the subject will be coming down at some point) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not quite sure what to say about this; what about the skateboarder''s right foot?  hands?  the background railing?  I thought all of these gave a real sense of motion to the pic, while keeping the gaze locked.  I will concede that having the guy in the background turned out to be a bit distracting to most voters.</td>', 'Originally posted by Citadel: Not really getting a feeling of panning in this shot. The guy in the background is also distracting. In fact he is the only evidence of motion in this shot (aside from the fact that the subject will be coming down at some point)   Not quite sure what to say about this; what about the skateboarder''s right foot?  hands?  the background railing?  I thought all of these gave a real sense of motion to the pic, while keeping the gaze locked.  I will concede that having the guy in the background turned out to be a bit distracting to most voters.', '2007-01-27 12:24:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3291332, 453816, 36988, '<td valign="top">Your first ribbon and so worthy. Great capture!</td>', 'Your first ribbon and so worthy. Great capture!', '2007-01-27 15:41:10.000000', NULL, 0),
