(3298262, 452479, 42100, '<td valign="top">Very vivid color in this photo, congratulations on winning the red ribbon Alex!</td>', 'Very vivid color in this photo, congratulations on winning the red ribbon Alex!', '2007-01-29 11:17:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3298264, 453974, 42100, '<td valign="top">Very nice photograph, congratulations on winning the yellow ribbon!</td>', 'Very nice photograph, congratulations on winning the yellow ribbon!', '2007-01-29 11:19:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299841, 454082, 40683, '<td valign="top">I like this one very much and I agree that it''s just right the way it is.  The slight blur of the silhouetted subject adds to the image IMO.  I must say though that I was so enjoying the mysterious mood that you conjured up which allowed for a lot of different stories to bounce around in my head, but then I read the title which spelled out for me what had been an intriguing unknown.  I think that such a deliciously moody image deserves more than one story.  Really do like it though.  :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-29 19:01:10.</i></td>', 'I like this one very much and I agree that it''s just right the way it is.  The slight blur of the silhouetted subject adds to the image IMO.  I must say though that I was so enjoying the mysterious mood that you conjured up which allowed for a lot of different stories to bounce around in my head, but then I read the title which spelled out for me what had been an intriguing unknown.  I think that such a deliciously moody image deserves more than one story.  Really do like it though.  :)', '2007-01-29 17:17:05.000000', '2007-01-29 19:01:10.000000', 0),
(3301507, 453495, 62318, '<td valign="top">Hmmm, this shot gives me ideas. I love when a shot does this. With a long focal length, an extremely long exposure (5 seconds or so), and keeping the panning on the cart the whole time I bet this would be tremendous. High speed background motion, perfectly focused cart, blurrly legs.... I might have to try this. Probably take a few hundred shots to get the cart in sharp focus for that long of an exposure. Three different senses of motion. A little off the critiquing really but just rambling things as they come to mind...<br/> <br/>Great ideas come from the simpliest photos.<br/> <br/>As for the photo itself in this challenge, I think it was a great idea just a bit hard to sell to the motion panning voters. Exposure was good, angle was terrific, and the technique of panning was strong (but short lived).</td>', 'Hmmm, this shot gives me ideas. I love when a shot does this. With a long focal length, an extremely long exposure (5 seconds or so), and keeping the panning on the cart the whole time I bet this would be tremendous. High speed background motion, perfectly focused cart, blurrly legs.... I might have to try this. Probably take a few hundred shots to get the cart in sharp focus for that long of an exposure. Three different senses of motion. A little off the critiquing really but just rambling things as they come to mind... Great ideas come from the simpliest photos. As for the photo itself in this challenge, I think it was a great idea just a bit hard to sell to the motion panning voters. Exposure was good, angle was terrific, and the technique of panning was strong (but short lived).', '2007-01-30 00:45:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3303892, 454082, 61348, '<td valign="top">Ohh this was one of the verry good of the motion panning<br/>gave it a 8 durring the vote <br/>I like so much the ambiance and the colours<br/> <br/>I think the picture wouldn''t be so nice if the person was sharp <br/> <br/>The only thing I doesn''t liek varry much is the orange part of the border</td>', 'Ohh this was one of the verry good of the motion panninggave it a 8 durring the vote I like so much the ambiance and the colours I think the picture wouldn''t be so nice if the person was sharp  The only thing I doesn''t liek varry much is the orange part of the border', '2007-01-30 17:00:57.000000', NULL, 0),
